  "prompt": "What conditions must a corporation satisfy to claim a bad debt as a deductible expense?",
  "runtimeCommit": "87ce0c7571f9bd57514b6c2dfb45e9427d19c6b6",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nTo claim a bad debt as a deductible expense, a corporation must demonstrate that the debt is considered worthless and that it has been previously included in gross income.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practice, this means that corporations must maintain adequate records to substantiate the worthlessness of the debt and its prior inclusion in income. This documentation is crucial for tax compliance and to support the deduction in case of an audit by the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR).",
